      {
        "ref": "2SA 2:8",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now Abner the son of Ner, captain of Saul’s army, had taken Ishbosheth the son of Saul and brought him over to Mahanaim."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA 2:12",
        "textualBasisJa": "Abner the son of Ner, and the servants of Ishbosheth the son of Saul, went out from Mahanaim to Gibeon."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA 3:23",
        "textualBasisJa": "When Joab and all the army who was with him had come, they told Joab, “Abner the son of Ner came to the king, and he has sent him away, and he has gone in peace.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA 3:25",
        "textualBasisJa": "You know Abner the son of Ner. He came to deceive you, and to know your going out and your coming in, and to know all that you do.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA 3:28",
        "textualBasisJa": "Afterward, when David heard it, he said, “I and my kingdom are guiltless before the LORD forever of the blood of Abner the son of Ner."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA 3:37",
        "textualBasisJa": "So all the people and all Israel understood that day that it was not of the king to kill Abner the son of Ner."
      }
    ],
